course: dictionary
lesson: 11579
title: Per annum: each year
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Annum is a Latin word that means year. You will almost never see it on its own. You will see it in the phrase «per annum», where per means for each. So per annum means for each year.
explain: Money and maths problems often use it. «The gym membership costs 300 pounds per annum.» This tells you the gym costs 300 pounds for one whole year, not for one month. To check, swap in «each year» and read the sentence again: «The gym membership costs 300 pounds each year.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: You may see it written short as p.a. «The bank pays 3% p.a. on savings» means the bank pays 3% every year. When you see per annum or p.a., stop and ask yourself: is this amount for one year, or for something shorter?
fact: Annum means year.
fact: «Per annum» means each year or for every year.
fact: «p.a.» is a short way of writing «per annum».
fact: Many English words and phrases come from Latin, an old language used by the Romans.
fact: Money problems often give a rate or a price per annum, so always check the time period before you work out the answer.
exercise: «The club costs 50 pounds per annum.» What does per annum mean here? | Each day | Only once | *Each year | Each month
exercise: The letters p.a. are short for which words? | per week | per hour | per month | *per annum
exercise: «The school trip happens once per annum.» How often does the trip happen? | Twice in one day | Every week | Every day | *Once a year
test: «The magazine costs 24 pounds per annum.» Does this price cover one month or one year? | One week | One hour | One day | *One year
test: Which phrase means the same as «per annum»? | per hour | *per year | per mile | per day
exam: Mia reads «The bank pays 3% p.a. on savings.» What is the best meaning of p.a. here? | only once ever | *each year | each hour | each morning
